Program Bug_2_07_SineAutoinitUnitOnly;
// Bug 2.7: Parser::InitBuiltinFunction (parser.cpp ~211-380) auto-inserts
// an up-front `jsr initsine_calculate` the first time it sees the literal
// text "sine[" - but it only scans `m_lexer->m_text`, the text of
// whichever parser/lexer instance is CURRENTLY active, which runs
// separately per file. If "sine[" only appears inside a `@use`d unit's own
// text, never repeated in the main .ras file's own text, the up-front jsr
// never gets emitted and nothing else ever calls it either, so
// InitSinusTable's 256-byte table sits as whatever memory already held
// forever, and every `sine[angle]` read is garbage, silently, with no
// compile error.
//
// Companion unit: 2_07_sine_autoinit_unit_only.tru (SineUnit::GetSine),
// whose only "sine[" usage is inside the unit's own function body - this
// main file never repeats the pattern itself.
//
// Verified via a static check on the generated .asm (see the companion
// .asmcheck file), not a runtime value: the table's own storage (`sine
// .byte 0` plus a following `org sine+#255`, no data bytes emitted)
// reserves 256 bytes without giving them a real compile-time value, so
// "uninitialized" isn't reliably 0 at runtime - VICE's own default RAM
// fill pattern can leave nonzero garbage there (confirmed live: an
// earlier version of this snippet asserting a bare "sine[64]<>0" false-
// PASSed even with the jsr genuinely absent). A same-file sentinel poke
// doesn't work either: the up-front jsr, when present, runs unconditionally
// at the very top of the program, before any of this file's own code -
// there's no source-level point after which a sentinel could still
// distinguish "never ran" from "already ran and we clobbered its result".
// The generated .asm text itself is the only reliable signal: confirmed
// live that `jsr initsine_calculate` is completely absent from the whole
// program in this unit-only-usage shape, while `jsr SineUnit_GetSine` (the
// actual call site) is present as expected.
@use "2_07_sine_autoinit_unit_only"

var
	v : byte;

begin
	v := SineUnit::GetSine(64);
	screen_bg_col := v;
	loop();
end.
